# Line endings.
#
# The index already stores text as LF. What produced the several thousand
# `Delete CR` warnings from Prettier and ESLint on Windows was the checkout:
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF in the working tree, and Prettier
# defaults to endOfLine: "lf", so every line of every affected file was flagged.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for this repository, so the working tree
# matches the index on every platform and the warnings stop at the source
# rather than being suppressed in the Prettier config. That matters because
# `npm run fmt:check` is a CI gate as of 14-08-2026, and CI checks out on Linux
# while the maintainer works on Windows. Without this the two disagree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts break outright with CRLF: the interpreter reads the carriage
# return as part of the shebang path and reports "No such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Binary, so Git never attempts line ending conversion or diffing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Marking them keeps them out of diff review noise
# while still storing them as LF text.
package-lock.json text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
bun.lock text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
